<title>USA: Illinois jobless rate for Nov. drops to 5 percent.</title>
<headline>Illinois jobless rate for Nov. drops to 5 percent.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Illinois' unemployment rate dropped for the third consecutive month in November to a seasonally adjusted five percent, the state's department of employment security reported Tuesday.</p>
<p>The five percent jobless rate, down from 5.1 percent in October and 5.2 percent in November 1995, was the lowest for the state in 20 months, the department said.</p>
<p>Jobless workers numbered 305,926 in November, compared to 316,833 in October, according to the report.</p>
<p>--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647</p>
</text>
